---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Header from '../../components/Header.astro'; import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'; import { siteContent } from '../../data/siteContent'; import '../../styles/aeo-experiment.css';
const { aeoExperiment } = siteContent;
const metrics=[['Baseline test date',aeoExperiment.baseline.date],['Model',aeoExperiment.baseline.model],['Prompt set',aeoExperiment.baseline.promptSet],['ChatGPT mentions',aeoExperiment.baseline.mentions],['AI Visibility Rate',aeoExperiment.baseline.visibilityRate],['Citation Rate',aeoExperiment.baseline.citationRate]];
---
<BaseLayout title="Sew What’s Next AEO Experiment | Mae Fang" description="A public Answer Engine Optimization experiment tracking whether Sew What’s Next can become discoverable in AI-generated answers for sewing planning and fabric stash queries."><Header/><main id="main-content" class="experiment-page page-shell"><a class="back-link" href="/#projects">← Back to selected work</a><header class="experiment-page-header"><p class="eyebrow">AI Search Lab · Public experiment</p><h1>Sew What’s Next AEO Experiment</h1><p>A measurable, public test of whether a new niche product can earn visibility in AI-generated answers.</p><div class="experiment-status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Baseline established · Experiment active</div></header>
<section><h2>Experiment Overview</h2><p>{aeoExperiment.description}</p><p>{aeoExperiment.process}</p></section>
<section><h2>Baseline</h2><p>The first frozen test establishes the starting point. These numbers do not claim improvement; they give future experiment rounds something consistent to compare against.</p><dl class="detail-metrics">{metrics.map(([label,value])=><div class="metric"><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
<section><h2>Methodology</h2><ol class="method-list"><li><strong>Establish a baseline</strong><span>Run a fixed set of 15 prompts and record mentions, citations, competitors, and answer patterns.</span></li><li><strong>Analyze competing answers</strong><span>Study the products and sources surfaced for sewing planning, fabric stash, and pattern-matching queries.</span></li><li><strong>Make targeted changes</strong><span>Improve first-party content and technical signals based on gaps revealed by the baseline.</span></li><li><strong>Rerun and document</strong><span>Repeat the frozen prompt set, compare results, and publish what changed.</span></li></ol></section>
<section><h2>Results Over Time</h2><div class="results-placeholder"><strong>Round 0 · Baseline</strong><span>August 15, 2026</span><p>0 of 15 ChatGPT prompts mentioned Sew What’s Next. Visibility and citation rates both began at 0%.</p></div></section>
<section><h2>What I’m Learning</h2><p>This page will become the source of record for the experiment. Future updates will separate observed changes from hypotheses and document both positive and negative results.</p></section></main><Footer/></BaseLayout>
